    "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#bidi-rendering says\r\n\r\n> Input fields (i.e. [textarea](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-textarea-element) elements, and [input](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-input-element) elements when their [type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-input-type) attribute is in the [Text](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)), [Search](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)), [Telephone](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#telephone-state-(type=tel)), [URL](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#url-state-(type=url)), or [Email](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#email-state-(type=email)) state) are expected to present an editing user interface with a directionality that matches the element's ['direction'](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes/#direction) property.\r\n\r\nWhile this doesn't say that users are expected to be able to change the directionality for these elements, it seems inconsistent to support author-provided directionality but only allow users to change directionality for a subset, or to allow changing directionality but then not submitting it with `dirname`.\r\n\r\n`hidden` may be useful as a way of submitting `contenteditable` elements.\r\n\r\nRelatedly, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#persisted-user-state-restoration also says to (optionally) restore `dir` attribute values in session restore:\r\n\r\n> Optionally, update other aspects of entry's [document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#she-document) and its rendering, for instance values of form fields, that the user agent had previously recorded in entry's [persisted user state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#she-other).\r\n>\r\n> Note: This can even include updating the [dir](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-dir) attribute of [textarea](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-textarea-element) elements or [input](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-input-element) elements whose [type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-input-type) attribute is in either the [Text](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)) state or the [Search](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)) state, if the persisted state includes the directionality of user input in such controls.\r\n\r\nThis note should probably be updated if we allow `dirname` on more elements.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
